nd advanced computing; and Xanadu Quantum Technologies Limited to accelerate utility-scale quantum manufacturing. The company was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in Malta, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Timothy Graham Breen | CEO & Director | Age 47","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $485K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $72K of free cash flow annually.","financial_summary":["GlobalFoundries Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $21.5B market cap on $6.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +3.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.95\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 8.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (92% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.077},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"News tone classified negative across 12 recent articles","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 37% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"GlobalFoundries (GFS) Stock May Be Near Fair Value On Its 35% Slide","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-gfs/globalfoundries/news/globalfoundries-gfs-stock-may-be-near-fair-value-on-its-35-s","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000128.921,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GFS or MRVL: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.